laurel 2920: the Mi A3 main microphone. Path from the stock tree + LineageOS mixer paths ("amic1"): AMIC1 + MIC BIAS1 1.8 V -> WCD937x ADC1 -> SoundWire TX (master 0x0a470000, slave 0x01170223, codec port 0 -> master port 2, 50 x 16 frame, si 3 off1 1) -> TX macro 0x0a460000 DEC0 -> AFE TX_CDC_DMA_TX_3 (0xB037, 48 kHz 16-bit mono, mask 1) -> ADM record COPP (NULL topology) -> ASM session 2 read, 8 x 20 ms periods in the pool (SID 0x41 identity, msw 1). Rails RPM L9A + L14A (no SPMI: the codec is a SoundWire device). Clocks AFE 0x30c + 0x30d 19.2 MHz: the macros are touched only after both are given. /dev/redwood-mic (the node RedwoodAudio.driver's "Codec" reads): open by the audio server (or root) starts the path, close stops it, read never waits, ioctl _IOW('r', 2) sets the capture gain (DEC0 digital gain 18 dB down to -6 dB). All on the audio thread; playback goes on between the steps. On by default; kill switch mic=0 (adsp=0 too); self-check at boot = the whole path once, 2 reads back in 500 ms; one line LAUREL MIC: on|off: reason; LAUREL MIC: first capture: rms N proves real samples. A failure turns off only the microphone (3 failed starts in a row: off). Details: docs/laurel_sprout/audio.md "Microphone".

